      <h2>About Palace Museum</h2>
      <p>Beit al-Sahel (Palace Museum) served as the Sultan&#x27;s official residence from the late 19th century until the 1964 revolution. The palace displays royal furniture, ceremonial regalia, portraits of sultans, historical photographs, and artifacts documenting Zanzibar&#x27;s sultanate era and the 1964 revolution. The building showcases classic Omani-Arab architecture with carved teak doors, ornate plasterwork, marble floors, and European-influenced chandeliers. Guided tours provide context on the sultanate&#x27;s political history and the 1964 revolution.</p>

